      "message": "**Issue #1 (🟡 Medium Severity (SHOULD FIX))**: `Delete All SNMP Managers` — IPv4-only parsing assumption is undocumented\n\n**Issue**: `Fetch From Left  ${ip_port}  :` splits on the first colon. For IPv4 (`10.6.6.6:162`) this correctly yields the IP. For an IPv6 literal (`[::1]:162`) it would yield `[` and produce a silently incorrect `Delete SNMP Manager Via Redfish` call. The limitation is undocumented, making it a maintenance hazard if IPv6 variables are ever added to `lib/snmp/resource.robot`.\n-\n\n**Fix**:\n```robot\n  # IPv4-only: Fetch From Left splits on the first colon; IPv6 addresses\n  # are not supported here, consistent with lib/snmp/resource.robot scope.\n  ${ip_port}\u003d  Fetch From Right  ${snmp_mgr}  snmp://\n  ${snmp_ip}\u003d  Fetch From Left   ${ip_port}  :\n  ${snmp_port}\u003d  Fetch From Right  ${ip_port}  :\n  ```\n\n**Why**: Makes the constraint visible to future contributors and prevents silent misbehaviour if IPv6 test variables are added later.",
